# Sceau's R8 rules. AGP combines all the files of src/main/keepRules.
# See https://d.android.com/r/tools/r8/keep-rules
# Rationale and measurements: docs/decisions.md, D24.

# BouncyCastle: the JCA provider loads its "$Mappings" classes by name
# (ClassUtil.loadClass then newInstance); these register each implementation
# (Cipher, Signature, KeyAgreement, KeyFactory, CertificateFactory, Mac...) as a class name,
# which Provider.Service instantiates by reflection with the public constructor (no argument,
# or with one parameter for CertStore). It is therefore enough to keep the names of these
# classes and their constructors: the methods called afterwards are overrides of Java SPIs
# (CipherSpi, SignatureSpi...) or of AlgorithmProvider.configure, which R8 keeps on its own
# for an instantiated class; the rest is shrunk and obfuscated. BC's other reflective calls
# (GcmSpecUtil, SpecUtil, DRBG...) target JDK classes, not code to keep.
-keep class org.bouncycastle.jcajce.provider.** { <init>(...); }
-keep class org.bouncycastle.jce.provider.** { <init>(...); }

# JMRTD, SCUBA and cert-cvc: no rule. Their only reflection is Country.values(), which calls
# values() on SCUBA's enums (covered by the enum rule of proguard-android-optimize),
# and CardService.getInstance / CVCProvider, which Sceau does not use (TransportCardService
# extends CardService directly). The algorithms they request by name go through
# BouncyCastle, covered above.

# BouncyCastle references JNDI (javax.naming) for the LDAP and DANE stores, absent
# from Android and never used by Sceau.
-dontwarn javax.naming.**

# Native JPEG 2000 decoder (libsceau_jp2.so): the JNI function is bound by the name of the class
# and of the native method, which must not be renamed.
-keepclasseswithmembernames,includedescriptorclasses class io.github.mgdx.sceau.jp2.Jpeg2000Decoder {
    native <methods>;
}
